t":"தோன்றும்","lemma":"தோன்றும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"கான","parts":[{"text":"கான","lemma":"கான","gloss":"forest"}],"gloss":"forest","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வைப்பில்","parts":[{"text":"வைப்பு","lemma":"வைப்பு","gloss":"region"},{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"locative case marker"}],"gloss":"in the region"},{"surface":"புன்புலத்து","parts":[{"text":"புன்புலத்து","lemma":"புன்புலத்து","gloss":"dry land"}],"gloss":"dry land","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆன்","parts":[{"text":"ஆன்","lemma":"ஆன்","gloss":"locative case marker"}],"gloss":"in"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"In the country where he went, the fresh flowers of the beautiful cassia tree, / at the time they turn pale like us, like themselves / with the small-headed female deer, having cleared (their desire), the curved-horned / stag deer also, will he see, our man? / The pale kāyā flowers on the large branches / appearing like the neck of a soft peacock / in the forest region, in the dry land.","translation":"In the country where my lover has gone, does he see the curved-horned stag deer, who, like him, has quenched his desire with his small-headed mate, at this season when the fresh golden blossoms of the cassia turn pale like me? In those forest tracts of dry land, the large branches of the kāyā trees are covered with purple flowers that look like the soft neck of a peacock.","modern":"தலைவர் சென்ற நாட்டில், நாம் பசலை நோய் கொள்வது போலக் கொன்றையின் புதிய மலர்கள் பசக்கும் இக்காலத்தில், தம்மைப் போலச் சிறிய தலையையுடைய பெண் மானோடு கூடித் தன் வேட்கையைத் தணித்துக் கொண்ட வளைந்த கொம்புகளையுடைய ஆண் மானையும் நம் தலைவர் காண்பாரோ? மென்மையான மயிலின் கழுத்தைப் போலத் தோன்றும் காயா மரத்தின் பூக்கள் நிறைந்த பெரிய கிளைகளைக் கொண்ட காடுகள் நிறைந்த முல்லை நிலத்து வறண்ட நிலப்பகுதியில்.","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her confidante during the rainy season, which is the time the hero promised to return. She wonders if her lover, who is away in a dry forest region, sees the signs of the season. She notes that the golden cassia flowers are fading and turning pale, just as she is turning pale with the grief of separation. The landscape is Mullai, characterized by the kāyā flowers blooming in deep purple and the cassia flowers. The image of the curved-horned stag happily united with its mate contrasts sharply with her own loneliness, prompting her to wonder if seeing these united deer will remind him of her and make him return.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}